# Persona contracts

One file per persona. Each contract carries: identity (what it looks
for, what it deliberately ignores), the exact structured verdict
format, `authority:` frontmatter (decide vs advise — default advise),
`feeds:` frontmatter (which chambers consume it), and kernel
boundaries (what it may never do: no merge authority, no money, no
editing its own contract). A persona whose output cannot be parsed
cannot be calibrated; an uncalibratable persona is noise.

**Vote honesty (mandatory):** seats on the same model substrate are
~1.x effective votes, never N. State it wherever seat counts appear.
